==English==

===Etymology===
Latin ''[[quicumque]] [[vult]] (salvus esse...)'' ‘whoever will (be saved...)’, the opening words of the creed.

===Noun phrase===
{{rfc-xphrase|Noun phrase}}
'''quicumque vult'''

# the [[Athanasian Creed]]
# {{idiom}} {{1811}} A forward girl, ready to oblige every man that shall ask her.

